Falsifies `designware_mobile_storage::proofs::the_master_boot_record_parse_is_total_and_reads_each_entry_from_its_own_bytes`.

The defect: an entry's length is read from the same four bytes as its start, so every partition is
reported as long as its start. A write test or a filesystem walk would then believe a partition
ends where it does not.

Expected to fail: the harness's assertion that `entry.sectors` equals the little-endian word at
offset 12 of its entry, on any sector 0 whose start and length words differ.

diff --git a/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/partition.rs b/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/partition.rs
--- a/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/partition.rs
+++ b/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/partition.rs
@@ -106,7 +106,7 @@
             *e = PartitionEntry {
                 kind: sector[at + 4],
                 start: le(8),
-                sectors: le(12),
+                sectors: le(8),
             };
         }
         Some(MasterBootRecord { entries })
